    description: "Excluded `dispatches_to` from `pick_reverse_slice_seeds`'s out-degree counting in `scripts/bakeoff-deep` (the prometheus genericSeriesSet.Err regression cited in the function's own comment had recurred — interface stubs picking up out=N from synthetic trait→impl edges and outranking real domain functions). 16 of 18 dispatches_to producers emit synthetic 'menu' relationships; the 2 real-dispatch producers (route_handler.py, grpc.py:790) score via the route + API-handler boosts already.\n\nValidation: next DEEP bakeoff cycle should show seed selection shifting away from interface stubs (e.g. SeriesSet.Err on prometheus, similar trait stubs on rust repos) toward real domain functions. `moved` if confirmed, `no_move` (parent-link a regression sub-item) if seeds get worse, `inconclusive` otherwise.\n\nTriggered by failed full-suite test `tests/test_bakeoff_deep_compress.py::test_pick_reverse_slice_seeds_dispatches_to_not_counted_as_out`. Fix lands via PR (number TBD)."  # 2853
    fields: {}  # 2853
